  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-llm-volcengine-plans",
      "text": "[English](README.md) | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nA community DeepSeek Harness bundle for Volcengine Ark Agent Plan and Coding Plan."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- Registers isolated `volcengine-plan/*` and `volcengine-coding/*` routes.\n- Publishes per-model context, output, modality, and thinking-level metadata.\n- Applies the OpenAI compatibility switches required by the Coding Plan gateway.\n- Resolves `ARK_API_KEY` through the DSH credential service on every request, with legacy variable fallbacks.\n- Provides a credential form under **Settings → Plugins → Plugin configuration**.\n- Supports validated, live-reloadable route, endpoint, header, timeout, retry, and default-reasoning configuration.\n- Avoids the unsupported third-party Models editor registration that broke DSH rc.6's Add provider dialog."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Install from GitHub:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:lionXiao/dsh-llm-volcengine-plans#v0.3.1\n```\n\nRestart DSH, then select a model such as `volcengine-coding/deepseek-v4-flash`. The old `dsh-llm-volcengine` package must not be installed alongside this bundle because both own the same routes."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "The package follows DSH's documented bundle manifest and the community `dsh-*` naming convention without using the reserved-looking `@deepseek-ai` scope. Add the `dsh-plugin` GitHub topic when publishing its repository."
    },
    {
      "section": "Credentials",
      "text": "The default credential reference is `ARK_API_KEY`, matching Volcengine's tool integration convention. A previously stored DSH credential under that reference is reused; the old plugin and a custom `ark` provider are not runtime dependencies."
    },
    {
      "section": "Credentials",
      "text": "After restarting DSH, open **Settings → Plugins → Plugin configuration → Volcengine Plans** to save, replace, or remove the key. The browser receives only its configured state; the secret is stored by DSH in `$DSH_HOME/.credentials.yaml` and is never returned to the form."
    },
    {
      "section": "Models and Thinking Levels",
      "text": "Select a `volcengine-plan/*` or `volcengine-coding/*` model in the model picker. Models whose endpoint supports it expose DSH's native thinking-level selector.\n\n| Model picker | Thinking-level picker |\n| --- | --- |\n|  |  |\n\nNever commit a real key. DSH can also read it from the launching environment or `$DSH_HOME/.env`:\n\n```dotenv\nARK_API_KEY=your_key\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "See `cordis.patch.yml` for defaults and `README.zh.md` for the complete configuration example and DSH rc.6 UI limitation."
    },
    {
      "section": "Verification",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm test\nnpm run pack:check\ndsh --profile web --dump-config\n```\n\nReal endpoint verification requires a user-supplied Volcengine key and is intentionally excluded from automated tests."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
